```plaintext
1result.sql
``` 

1result.sql is chosen because  
• it finds the previous non‑zero volume with a single window function (MAX … OVER), so the lookup is guaranteed to ignore zero volumes and is executed once for the whole data set rather than through a row‑by‑row correlated sub‑query (which 0result.sql uses and is less efficient).  
• after the previous‑volume logic is complete it simply filters the final result to 1‑10 Aug 2021, giving the requested rows in the correct ticker/date order.  
• all cleaning rules (K → ×1 000, M → ×1 000 000, ‘‑’ → 0) are applied in one clear CASE expression.  
Hence 1result.sql satisfies the specification more cleanly and efficiently than 0result.sql.